.TH ECHO\-AI 1 2026-07-23 "Echo AI" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
echo\-ai \- agentic AI system with conversational frontend
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B echo\-ai
[\fB\-\-web\fR] [\fB\-\-cli\fR] [\fB\-\-chat\fR]
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIPATH\fR] [\fB\-\-debug\fR]
[\fB\-\-help\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Echo AI is an agentic AI system with a conversational frontend and a tool-using backend.
It runs a HTTP/WebSocket server (default) or an interactive CLI REPL.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-web
Start the HTTP server on port 8080 (default).
.TP
.B \-\-cli
Start the interactive CLI REPL.
.TP
.B \-\-chat
Start lightweight chat mode (not yet implemented).
.TP
.B \-\-config \fIPATH\fR
Path to configuration file (default: \fBconfig.conf\fR).
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable debug-level logging to stderr.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Display this help message and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Echo AI uses a custom \fB.conf\fR format. See \fBconfig.conf.example\fR for a complete reference.
.P
Configuration is loaded from \fBconfig.conf\fR in the current directory by default.
Use \fB\-\-config\fR to specify a different path.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B ECHO_PASSWORD
Encryption password for session persistence. If not set, the server reads from
\fB~/.config/echo\-ai/password\fR. If neither is available, session persistence is skipped
and the server runs in unlocked mode (frontend handles password entry).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/echo\-ai/password
Optional password file for session encryption.
.TP
.I ~/.config/echo\-ai/salt
Scrypt salt file (auto-generated on first run).
.TP
.I ~/.config/echo\-ai/.verifier
Encrypted verifier token for password validation.
.TP
.I ~/.config/echo\-ai/sessions/
Directory containing encrypted session data.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.B libuv,
.B libcurl,
.B sqlite3,
.B openssl,
.B cJSON
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at https://github.com/barontek/echo-ai-c/issues
